  <office:master-styles><style:master-page style:name="Standard" style:page-layout-name="pm1"/></office:master-styles>
  <office:body><office:text><text:p text:style-name="Title">Pictures from the Fictional Fair</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">An inline badge <draw:frame draw:style-name="frImage" draw:name="Badge" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="1cm" svg:height="1cm" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image><office:binary-data></office:binary-data></draw:image></draw:frame> sits inside this sentence, followed by more text. Each volunteer described the tidal patterns of the northern bay with remarkable patience. The harbour office mapped the songs sung at the autumn market with remarkable patience.</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Centered"><draw:frame draw:style-name="frImage" draw:name="Chart" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="9cm" svg:height="6cm" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image><office:binary-data>iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAADwAAAAoCAIAAAAt2Q6oAAAAWUlEQVR42u3YMRGAMBBE0SiJAVKlwwxOoiGW4iwYYK6i4Ib3ZwW8ektJ2k4VNDT0e9XRg0FDQ+dFt2sGg4aGhoaGhn5Gr/MIBg0NDQ0NDQ0NDf0v9NdP9XTd1V3sGtG5X5cAAAAASUVORK5CYII=</office:binary-data></draw:image></draw:frame></text:p><text:p text:style-name="Caption">Figure 1. Invented visitor numbers for three stalls.</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"><draw:frame draw:style-name="frWrap" draw:name="Landscape" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:width="6cm" svg:height="4cm" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image><office:binary-data></office:binary-data></draw:image></draw:frame>The survey team measured the songs sung at the autumn market without any modern instruments. The survey team questioned the tidal patterns of the northern bay using only paper notebooks. Every visiting student measured the tidal patterns of the northern bay with remarkable patience. The Brindlemoor committee summarised the condition of the wooden pier without any modern instruments. The archive keeper reviewed the colours of the evening sky over the dunes using only paper notebooks. The lighthouse crew estimated the growth of moss on the old stone walls using only paper notebooks.</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">The lighthouse crew measured the number of lanterns repaired each winter for the annual report. The Brindlemoor committee reviewed the number of lanterns repaired each winter using only paper notebooks. A small working group estimated the colours of the evening sky over the dunes for the annual report. The lighthouse crew compared the number of lanterns repaired each winter despite the persistent fog.</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Standard"><draw:frame draw:style-name="frBlock" draw:name="ChartBlock" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:width="12cm" svg:height="8cm" draw:z-index="0"><draw:image><office:binary-data>iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAADwAAAAoCAIAAAAt2Q6oAAAAWUlEQVR42u3YMRGAMBBE0SiJAVKlwwxOoiGW4iwYYK6i4Ib3ZwW8ektJ2k4VNDT0e9XRg0FDQ+dFt2sGg4aGhoaGhn5Gr/MIBg0NDQ0NDQ0NDf0v9NdP9XTd1V3sGtG5X5cAAAAASUVORK5CYII=</office:binary-data></draw:image></draw:frame></text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">The lighthouse crew estimated the weight of the fishing nets after each trip without any modern instruments. Each volunteer recorded the amount of rain collected in copper gauges in a careful and orderly way. The Brindlemoor committee questioned the number of lanterns repaired each winter before the season ended. Every visiting student questioned the growth of moss on the old stone walls in a careful and orderly way.</text:p></office:text></office:body>
</office:document>
